questions.answer:
First find the local field:
\[
g=G\frac{M}{r^2}
=\frac{(6.67\times10^{-11})(7.0\times10^{22})}{(2.0\times10^6)^2}
=1.17\,\mathrm{N\,kg^{-1}}
\]
Then
\[
W=mg=25(1.17)=29.2\,\mathrm{N}
\]

The field magnitude at the lander is
\[
g=\frac{W}{m}=\frac{300}{50}=6.0\,\mathrm{N\,kg^{-1}}
\]
For a spherical source,
\[
g=G\frac{M}{r^2}
\]
so
\[
M=\frac{gr^2}{G}
=\frac{6.0(8.0\times10^6)^2}{6.67\times10^{-11}}
=5.8\times10^{24}\,\mathrm{kg}
\]
